<div class="whatsnew">
  <h3>What is new in version {{ release.version }} ({{ release.date }}) {{ q('whatsnew') }}</h3>
  <p class="small" style="margin:0 0 6px">Everything added since the first release, grouped by what it lets you do.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Choose targets with better evidence.</strong> Independent evidence from mutations, copy number, cell-line dependency, a second cohort, kinase activity and tumour purity feeds two separate scores, one for targets and one for biomarkers, each with a rank interval from 1,000 random re-weightings (Candidates and Validation tabs).</li>
    <li><strong>Trust the text.</strong> Every sentence the agents write is checked against the evidence it cites: the record must exist, belong to that gene, and match the numbers and the up or down wording. A sentence is also dropped if its evidence changed after the agent read it.</li>
    <li><strong>Predict treatment response.</strong> Two clinical trials (IMmotion150 and Choueiri 2016) give progression and response results for every gene. Two published signatures reproduce, so the data work. No single gene separates immunotherapy from sunitinib once testing is corrected for (Treatment &amp; subtypes tab).</li>
    <li><strong>Look inside the tumour.</strong> Tumours are split by VHL, PBRM1, BAP1 and SETD2 mutation and by ccA or ccB subtype. The ccA/ccB difference is also part of the biomarker profile.</li>
    <li><strong>Judge antibody and radioligand targets.</strong> Surface proteins are scored on topology, increase in tumour, staining in vital organs and how evenly tumour cells carry them (ADC &amp; immune tab).</li>
    <li><strong>See the immune neighbourhood.</strong> Cold, intermediate and hot tumours feed an immune-target profile. A second single-cell dataset checks the cell-type calls.</li>
    <li><strong>Replicate the protein data.</strong> A separate confirmatory cohort of patients, measured with a different method, repeats the protein and phosphosite tests (Validation tab).</li>
    <li><strong>See the tissue.</strong> The Tissue viewer draws spots on real H&amp;E sections and shows the neighbours of any gene's high spots.</li>
    <li><strong>A fifth agent.</strong> A translational agent now writes findings on treatment response, subtypes, antibody-drug conjugates, the immune microenvironment and replication.</li>
    <li><strong>Count prior work better.</strong> Literature counts use only aliases that belong to one gene, and potent compounds and patent records from ChEMBL reduce the "undrugged" credit.</li>
    <li><strong>One criterion changed after seeing data.</strong> A selective dependency now needs at least three dependent ccRCC cell lines. Before, one or two of 24 lines could carry the call. It is logged as a post-hoc change in <code>evals/history.md</code>.</li>
  </ul>
</div>
